---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description="What this playground is.">
  <section class="flex flex-col gap-4">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight">About</h1>
    <p class="text-ink/80">
      This is a small blog whose sources live in a database, not on a disk. A Durable
      Object holds every file you see in the editor and hands them to a renderer running
      in the same isolate.
    </p>
    <p class="text-ink/80">
      There is no build step between your edit and the page. Save a file and the next
      request compiles it, runs it and returns HTML — usually in a few tens of
      milliseconds.
    </p>
    <ul class="flex flex-col gap-2 text-ink/80">
      <li><span class="font-medium text-ink">Pages</span> — file-based routes under src/pages</li>
      <li><span class="font-medium text-ink">Content</span> — markdown validated by a Zod schema</li>
      <li><span class="font-medium text-ink">Styles</span> — Tailwind v4, plus scoped CSS per component</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="text-ink/80">
      Try it: open <code class="rounded bg-ink/5 px-1 py-0.5 text-sm">src/styles/global.css</code>
      and change <code class="rounded bg-ink/5 px-1 py-0.5 text-sm">--color-signal</code> to
      something loud.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
